%description:

Tcp.delayedAckTimeout:invalid -- a negative value stops the run with an error at the open.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "with delayedAcksEnabled, the longest delay of an ACK (RFC 9293 MUST-40:
less than 0.5 s); 0 or more, 0s: no delay".

The classes: value (a positive time), zero (0s: no delay) and invalid (a negative value). The
code: TcpAlgorithm::initialize() reads the value at the open of each connection and stops the
run for a negative value, which would else reach the scheduler. This test separates "invalid" from the other classes.

Host under test: host2, with the value -1s; host1 opens a connection to host2 at 0.1 s. Observation:
level 0, the run stops at the open of the connection with the error of the check.

%# parameter: Tcp.delayedAckTimeout
%# class: invalid
%# value: -1s
%# key: *.host2.tcp.delayedAckTimeout
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpDelayedAckTimeoutInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.delayedAckTimeout = -1s    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
delayedAckTimeout must be 0 or more, but it is -1
